{
  "id": "edit-vs-delete",
  "title": "One device edits a note while another deletes it",
  "covers": [
    "spec: Deletes - tombstones; a delete beats an older edit",
    "ticket: edit vs delete"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "B deletes note N at T+20. A, offline, edits its tags at T+10 (older than the delete) and its meaning at T+30 (newer), reviews its card at T+31 and suspends the card at T+32.",
    "The delete wins against BOTH edits: deletion is permanent, so even the newer edit does not bring the note back.",
    "The edits are still applied to the tombstone's registers (so every replica holds the same row), the review is still inserted, the card row itself is not tombstoned but is hidden because its note is deleted.",
    "Nothing is rejected and A sees the note disappear after its next pull."
  ],
